From 460fbbf71a5b64766ab8faddf26392fd6eb45ed1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nsbradley88 <3960699+nsbradley88@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:23:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/15] vulkan: MMVQ (q8_1 integer dot) for IQ3_S, IQ3_XXS,
 IQ2_S, IQ2_XS

These types had only the float mat-vec path, which degrades fast with columns (MTP verify batches). The new
mmvq_dot_product functions decode one 32-value group per call (grid lookup, sign bits applied as a byte-wise
two's complement, all grid values are >= 1) and use dotPacked4x8EXT against the q8_1 activations, like IQ4_XS.
Rows per workgroup: 1 at n <= 4, 2 above on RDNA3/4 (env GGML_VK_IQ3_ROWS=AxB to override, A for n <= 4, B
above). Env GGML_VK_NO_IQ3_MMVQ=1 / GGML_VK_NO_IQ2_MMVQ=1 keep the float path (A/B).

Cold matvec, Radeon 8060S (gfx1151), 17408x5120, us at n = 1 / 5 / 8, float -> MMVQ:
  iq3_s   201 / 336 / 502 -> 197 / 248 / 301
  iq3_xxs 183 / 318 / 460 -> 175 / 229 / 288
  iq2_s   190 / 340 / 467 -> 182 / 233 / 309
  iq2_xs  160 / 323 / 455 -> 152 / 217 / 295
Numerics change (q8_1 activations, as for every other MMVQ type): Qwen3.8-27B UD-IQ4_XS KLD vs the Q8_0
reference through the 5-column path (llama-perplexity -ub 5, 4 chunks) 0.02441 +- 0.00133 -> 0.02461 +- 0.00138,
same top p 95.86 -> 95.94 %.
test-backend-ops: cold verify-shape perf cases for the UD-IQ4_XS mix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
